"In 1831, the English scientist Michael Faraday discovered something amazing. When he moved a magnet near a coil of wire, electricity flowed in the wire. When the magnet stopped, the electricity stopped too. A magnet sitting still does nothing; it is the change, the movement, that pushes the electrons. This is called electromagnetic induction, and almost every power plant in the world depends on it.": "fea3386e798d",
